Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Build Failures
Problem: Execution Environment build fails with dependency errors.

Solution:

# Check build logs for specific errors
ansible-builder build --tag custom-ee:debug --verbosity 3 .

# Common fixes:
# 1. Update base image
sed -i 's/ubi8/ubi9/g' execution-environment.yml

# 2. Fix Python package versions
echo "requests==2.28.2" >> requirements.txt

# 3. Add missing system dependencies
echo "python3-dev [platform:rpm]" >> bindep.txt
Issue 2: Upload/Push Failures
Problem: Cannot push to Private Automation Hub registry.

Solution:

# Verify registry connectivity
curl -k https://hub.example.com/v2/

# Re-authenticate
podman logout hub.example.com
podman login hub.example.com

# Check image size (large images may timeout)
podman images --format "table {{.Repository}} {{.Tag}} {{.Size}}"

# Try pushing with different timeout
podman push --timeout 300 hub.example.com/custom-ee:latest
Issue 3: Execution Environment Not Available in Controller
Problem: Custom EE doesn't appear in Automation Controller.

Solution:

# Verify EE is properly registered
curl -u admin:password \
  https://controller.example.com/api/v2/execution_environments/ \
  --insecure | jq '.results[] | {name, image}'

# Check pull policy and credentials
# Ensure Controller can access the registry
# Verify image name and tag are correct
Issue 4: Job Failures with Custom EE
Problem: Jobs fail when using the custom Execution Environment.

Solution:

# Check job output for specific errors
# Common issues:
# 1. Missing collections - add to requirements.yml
# 2. Python import errors - add to requirements.txt
# 3. System command not found - add to bindep.txt

# Test EE locally first
podman run --rm -it custom-ee:latest ansible --version
podman run --rm -it custom-ee:latest python3 -c "import requests; print('OK')"
